※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=64 diag=none

※ A sum of the widest signed type that will not fit stops the program too.
※ There is nowhere wider to compute it in, so what says it went past is the
※ sign the answer came out with: two numbers of one sign whose sum has the
※ other.  Both operands here are the same number, which is the case that asks
※ the question of the right pair of values or does not ask it at all.

let big: i64 = 9000000000000000000i64

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    if big + big = big:
        1u8
    else:
        2u8
